# Universe content · stars
# researched: Wikipedia "Stellar classification", plus each kind's own article for surface temperatures (Morgan–Keenan system, luminosity classes, extended classes C, S, L, T, Y, D)
# Real seeds for the star generator, plus its rules.
# Values are typical ranges from real astronomy. Spec: docs/CONTENT-FORMAT.md

# ── Main-sequence stars (the seven classic types) ──

# radius-sol: real radius ranges in Sun radii (standard astronomy references, rounded); a red supergiant can be
#   over 100,000 times wider than a neutron star, billions of times by volume.

# surface-kind: how its face is drawn: giant (a few huge convection cells, as in Betelgeuse), brown-dwarf (banded clouds),
#   white-dwarf (small, smooth), neutron-star (tiny), normal. spots: dark starspots (stars with deep convective layers: G, K, M
#   and young T Tauri stars). remnant: what is left when a star dies (white dwarfs, neutron stars, pulsars, magnetars).
@star o-type
name: O-type blue star
surface-kind: normal
real: yes
color: blue
temp-k: 30000..50000
mass-sol: 16..90
life-years: 1e6..1e7
share-of-stars: rarest
death: supernova
tags: hot, bright, short-lived, ultraviolet
radius-sol: 6.6..15

@star b-type
name: B-type blue-white star
surface-kind: normal
real: yes
color: blue-white
temp-k: 10000..30000
mass-sol: 2.1..16
life-years: 1e7..3e8
share-of-stars: rare
death: supernova at the heavy end, white dwarf at the light end
tags: hot, bright
radius-sol: 1.8..6.6

